<title>GERMANY: FOCUS-Allianz confident despite Ergo merger.</title>
<headline>FOCUS-Allianz confident despite Ergo merger.</headline>
<byline>Gernot Heller</byline>
<dateline>MUNICH, Germany 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>German insurer Allianz AG Holding said on Thursday it did not feel endangered as market leader by a recent key merger in the German insurance market and predicted a profit rise in 1997.</p>
<p>&quot;We do not see our position threatened,&quot; Allianz chairman Henning Schulte-Noelle told a news conference, referring to the consequences of the merger of insurers DKV and Hamburg-Mannheimer with Victoria Holding AG.</p>
